``` PHP2Shell (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619)
    Query 03. A PHP or web server process starting a shell, interpreter or download tool.
    This is the clearest sign that an attack worked.
    Data      CIM Endpoint data model, fed by your EDR or Sysmon for Linux.
    Schedule  Every hour with earliest=-1h. For the first run, use earliest="10/20/2026:00:00:00".
    Severity  High
    Tuning    Some apps start shells for image or PDF tools. Compare with what each host did before 20 October 2026. ```
| tstats summariesonly=false count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
    from datamodel=Endpoint.Processes
    where Processes.parent_process_name IN ("php*", "httpd", "apache2", "lsphp", "frankenphp")
      Processes.process_name IN ("sh", "bash", "dash", "curl", "wget", "python", "python3", "perl", "nc", "ncat", "socat", "base64")
      earliest=-1h
    by Processes.dest Processes.user Processes.parent_process_name Processes.process_name Processes.process
| rename Processes.* AS *
| search NOT process="*sendmail*"
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
